      "writtenOn": "2021-11-20T02:20:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "When these were first added to CommandBuffer, I had asked Jim if they could just take const Buffer* + size_t (or BindBufferInfo), but there was concern that we weren\u0027t accurately conveying ownership transfer. Having the main API on CB use sk_sp makes it clear that the CB will be reff\u0027ing these.\n\nThat being said, the bindDrawBuffers below is very convenient for the DrawWriter, which is why I added it. I am also not sure, but would believe that if we restricted everything to use DrawPass + DrawWriter / DBM for buffer management and binding, then we wouldn\u0027t have to worry about buffers not actually being transferred to the CB (since DBM does that in bulk).\n\nMy vote would be to keep this as-is for now, and revisit refs/lifecycle of all tracked resources for CBs/DrawPasses at a later point.",
      "parentUuid": "59b0c733_b3ceaa6f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 78,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 80,
        "endChar": 73
