      "writtenOn": "2021-11-19T19:22:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why is this needed to be declared in the class here? Similar question for SortKey.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 77,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 77,
        "endChar": 17
      },
      "revId": "ee1ca20dfc33f0422846b49c3b298bddf5db002b",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f9285de7_fdb956e8",
        "filename": "experimental/graphite/src/DrawPass.h",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 77,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-11-20T02:20:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "SortKey is declared here so that it can inherit the friend relationship between DrawList and DrawPass and be able to point to DrawList::Draw.\n\nDrawer eventually will need to record the command structs that DrawPass holds on to. Initially, I\u0027ve been having all of these structs private, since DrawPass creates them and handles converting them to appropriate calls to CommandBuffer in addCommands. If/when we move to Recordings holding on to DrawPasses directly and executing a task requires one virtual to then iterate over the DrawPass commands, these structs will necessarily be public and then I would bet Drawer could be a cpp only class.",
      "parentUuid": "45f5bb3a_e710a38c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 77,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 77,
        "endChar": 17
      },
      "revId": "ee1ca20dfc33f0422846b49c3b298bddf5db002b",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7373cd04_94ae2e7f",
        "filename": "experimental/graphite/src/DrawWriter.h",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 180,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-11-19T18:27:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "These aren\u0027t going to be batchable, but that\u0027s okay, since the only way they would have been is if the explicitly provided buffers happened to be contiguous, and in those sorts of situations, the RenderStep probably should have been using the append API anyways.\n\nThat being said, if it turns out we do make lots of contiguous explicit instance buffers, we can have drawInternal() handle the buffer checking and instance count incrementing instead of appendData().\n\nRight now, this just gives us a single type that needs to be passed to RenderStep\u0027s writeVertices() and RS can then choose how to handle its draws. I think it\u0027s reasonable to refine this as we learn more about the needs of the tessellating render steps that will be added later.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 166,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 180,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "ee1ca20dfc33f0422846b49c3b298bddf5db002b",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a98b18d8_a11d0472",
        "filename": "experimental/graphite/src/DrawWriter.h",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 217,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-11-19T18:27:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We might not need DrawWriter to take care of this logic, it could always set the buffers on the DrawDispatcher.\n\nMtlCommandBuffer already has logic to only actually record binds when there is a change. We could do something similar in the DrawPass\u0027 dispatcher as well.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 209,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 217,
        "endChar": 44
      },
      "revId": "ee1ca20dfc33f0422846b49c3b298bddf5db002b",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "448da2c7_8e029dc3",
        "filename": "experimental/graphite/src/DrawWriter.h",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 217,
      "author": {
        "id": 5036
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-11-19T19:08:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ideally I think we should not rely on the backends to not do a bind buffer. I would actually support down the line moving the checks in the backend command buffers to just be asserts that we aren\u0027t doing the same bind twice.",
      "parentUuid": "a98b18d8_a11d0472",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 209,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 217,
        "endChar": 44
      },
      "revId": "ee1ca20dfc33f0422846b49c3b298bddf5db002b",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "701dacf3_6df19124",
        "filename": "experimental/graphite/src/DrawWriter.h",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 217,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-11-20T02:20:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ok, I like that direction too. \n\nI will leave the buffer tracking in DrawWriter for now. If DrawDispatcher goes away entirely, we may gain some cleanup here to have DrawPass track the bound buffers, but I agree that it would be nice to let CommandBuffer be as dumb as possible.",
      "parentUuid": "448da2c7_8e029dc3",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 209,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 217,
        "endChar": 44
      },
      "revId": "ee1ca20dfc33f0422846b49c3b298bddf5db002b",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "946f9964_c33aebbd",
        "filename": "experimental/graphite/src/render/StencilAndFillPathRenderer.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 74,
      "author": {
        "id": 5036
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-11-19T19:22:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why are we passing in a ResourceProvider here? The only resource i could think we\u0027d need here is if we need to allocate a new buffer. But that should be handled by DrawBufferManager in the DrawWriter right?\n\nMy worry here is if anyone starts trying to get new resources at this stage in the recorder causing a lot of cross thread calls needing to happen to the resource cache.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 74,
        "startChar": 43,
        "endLine": 74,
        "endChar": 60
      },
      "revId": "ee1ca20dfc33f0422846b49c3b298bddf5db002b",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6724bd24_56beb185",
        "filename": "experimental/graphite/src/render/StencilAndFillPathRenderer.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 74,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-11-20T02:20:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I added ResourceProvider to \"writeVertices\" so that there was a way for RenderSteps to get at \"static\"/re-usable buffers that they may need, e.g. an index pattern.\n\nHowever, when that buffer hasn\u0027t been made yet, using the DBM is a lot nicer from their point of view (something I ran into in updating tests in a later CL). It doesn\u0027t seem out of this world to have DBM have a way to get at named/singleton buffers that a RenderStep \"owns\", since it internally can go to the ResourceProvider if necessary and return a vertex writer to fill it out.\n\nI think what I will do is let DrawWriter return the DBM that it is using, so that RenderSteps can get at that if they need to manually make buffers, and then completely remove the REsourceProvider argument here.",
      "parentUuid": "946f9964_c33aebbd",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 74,
        "startChar": 43,
        "endLine": 74,
        "endChar": 60
      },
